    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d746">

                <pb facs="0960" n="946" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg946"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856E.01/6–1047: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Baruch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-06-10T18:00:00+01:00">June 10, 1947—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>388. Foreign Minister considers note unsatisfactory in many respects after
                    further study. States official answer will await arrival tomorrow Commissioners
                    Schermerhorn and Van Poll, Batavia when Van Mook and Commissioners will give
                    full consideration and wire <pb facs="0961" n="947" xml:id="pg947"/> their
                    determination for discussion Cabinet here. His personal reaction is that answer
                    again totally disregards importance of federation and approach to United States
                    of Indonesia and over-emphasizes Republicans’ position and exaggerates its
                    importance in total Indonesian situation. Says Van Mook has already wired State
                    Department through Foote that his visit would not be helpful now and had best be
                    deferred. Thinks Saturday or Sunday<anchor n="7" xml:id="d746-f1"/> would be
                    earliest date reply from Commissioners could be expected here. I think his
                    personal views coincide closely with those of other Cabinet members.</p>
                <p>Sent Department as 388, repeated London as 41.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baruch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
